WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.770
One of the preferred and primary strategies
for Republicans to win elections for a long

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.040
time has been suppress the vote, make it more
difficult for people, especially people who

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.260
are less likely to vote for Republicans to
vote.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.350
And this has been done a whole bunch of different
ways of reducing the number of polling places,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.590
reducing early voting, purging people from
voter rolls.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.679
There's a very long list of tactics we've
talked about over the years, and the 2020

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:29.580
strategy is going to be really suppress the
vote even more than usual.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.260
We've already started to see it in some primaries
around the country and local elections.

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:39.440
And Kentucky is scheduled to have a primary
tomorrow and we may well be seeing the exact

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:40.480
same thing.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:46.170
Now, normally there are thirty seven hundred
polling places in Kentucky.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.640
Tomorrow there will be 200.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.030
You didn't hear that wrong?

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.030
Thirty seven hundred.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.060
There will be 200.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.969
That's a 95 percent reduction in polling places.

00:00:54.969 --> 00:00:58.710
Now, there's a double edged sword here and
the right wingers are trying to play both

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.670
sides of the coin, so to speak.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:05.820
And the reason that's being given for this
reduction in polling places is because of

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.100
the corona virus pandemic.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.020
A lot of poll workers don't want to work if
you can't staff polling places.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.190
You have to close them.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.910
Now, that is certainly plausible.

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:21.940
The problem is that in that case, you have
to ensure that people can vote by mail.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:26.710
You have to increase capacity dramatically
at the polling places that will be open.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.090
And there are widespread reports that people
who requested absentee ballots haven't received

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.090
them.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:33.820
And it's the day before they have to be mailed
out.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.410
They'd have to be postmarked by tomorrow,
Election Day.

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:42.250
So understand that on one hand, they are pretending
to respect the virus.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:43.830
You can't put people in harm's way.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:44.830
Great.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:48.390
I mean, I'm totally with you as far as that
goes, but they're not doing what needs to

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:53.860
be done to make sure people can vote by mail
or vote early, which is exactly what Republicans,

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:57.900
including Kentucky Republican Senator Mitch
McConnell, who's up for reelection.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.620
By the way, in November, and his his challenger
is going to be determined in this primary

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.620
tomorrow.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:04.730
That's what McConnell wants.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.560
That's what Donald Trump wants as well.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.270
Now, some early voting has been enabled.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:15.240
They at least claim that they're trying to
keep up with requests for absentee ballots.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.890
But it's just not working.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:22.810
And this is it's sort of a Hanlon's razor
situation, never a tribute to malice, that

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:28.170
which is adequately explained by stupidity
or I might say incompetence.

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.380
They claim that they did everything right.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.440
Not enough poll workers.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.700
So they said, hey, vote by mail, request absentee
ballots.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.860
There's going to be some early voting, et
cetera.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:42.040
A residents were sent postcards explaining
how mail in voting will work.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:46.180
Early voting has been available in some places
since June 8th.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:49.891
And the media and the governor, they've all
been telling everybody that this is this is

00:02:49.891 --> 00:02:50.970
going on.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:54.040
So there are people saying we did everything
we could.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.040
We really did.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.610
Given the circumstances.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:03.120
But at the same time, you know, when you read
that half of Kentucky's black voters live

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:11.220
in one county and that county will have one
polling place, that's rarely a coincidence

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:14.100
when we see that type of thing around the
country.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:20.319
So while I don't want to attribute to malice
that which can be adequately explained by

00:03:20.319 --> 00:03:26.600
incompetence or stupidity or ignorance, when
you read that half of the black population

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:30.710
is in one county which will have one polling
place, it doesn't sound good.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.080
It doesn't sound good.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.260
And certainly to some degree they were unprepared.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:40.990
I'm reading that instead of the normal three
to five days that it takes to receive an absentee

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:44.790
ballot application, some are taking upwards
of 20 days.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.340
I've gotten emails from people in Kentucky
under that situation.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:50.340
So what will happen tomorrow?

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:53.650
Well, we know what's going to happen, whether
it's malice or incompetence.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.210
Tomorrow you are going to have overcrowding
post polling places that are open.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:01.320
The ones that are open are going to be absolutely
busting at the seams up.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.690
People will not have received their absentee
ballots in many cases, and they will have

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:12.680
to decide, do I go out and risk catching the
virus and maybe waiting hours and hours at

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.670
a completely overloaded polling place?

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:20.070
Or do I just not vote because I didn't receive
an absentee ballot in the mail?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:24.030
And then you will have a situation that will
be similar to or even worse than the one we

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.340
saw in Georgia just a few weeks ago.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:29.960
So there are some important decisions to be
made tomorrow in Kentucky.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.910
There is, again, a Democratic primary race
to decide who will be facing off against Mitch

00:04:34.910 --> 00:04:37.690
McConnell in November.

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:40.940
There is Amy Magrath Charles Booker and some
other candidates.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.180
That's a big decision.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:48.000
There are some interesting House primaries
as well for the eventual November House of

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.310
Representatives elections happening in Kentucky.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.810
So this isn't nothing.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:56.460
And again, it's all a preview of what's going
to happen in November.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.220
The turnout tomorrow is not going to be as
big.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:02.570
As the number of people that will vote in
November, because you will have everybody

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:09.030
coming out to vote for either Joe Biden or
Donald Trump, if you see chaos tomorrow, multiply

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:13.470
by 50 to imagine what it is that's going to
be happening in November.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.850
Again, is it by design?

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:16.850
Is it incompetence?

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.900
Is it stupidity?

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.300
I don't know for sure.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.419
It's often a competent combination of all
of the above.

00:05:22.419 --> 00:05:22.539
Let me know what you think.

